WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.258
Stage three: the plan that says no.

2
00:00:05.108 --> 00:00:09.486
Monday, September twenty-eighth: the coach drafts Camille's week.

3
00:00:09.586 --> 00:00:14.348
Threshold Tuesday, hills Wednesday, long run Saturday.

4
00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:18.202
First, a second opinion. Computed, not guessed.

5
00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:25.830
Four guardrails measure load. Projected load ratio: one point one eight, under one point three.

6
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:31.124
Volume up six percent, elevation under five: both below ten.

7
00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:34.330
Monotony: one point six, under two.

8
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:41.718
No quality session after a red health verdict: none here. It's the only guardrail that blocks.

9
00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:48.284
The long run is thirty-nine percent of volume, above thirty-five: a warning, not a block.

10
00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:53.296
Seventh guardrail: quality on consecutive days.

11
00:00:53.396 --> 00:00:57.150
Threshold Tuesday, hills Wednesday: warning.

12
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.172
Hills move to Thursday, the easy run to Wednesday.

13
00:01:02.022 --> 00:01:08.056
The change is written to a decision file: the rule that fired, the before, the after.

14
00:01:11.022 --> 00:01:14.656
Every session gets targets computed for Camille.

15
00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:20.094
Heart rate zone, slope-adjusted pace, and expected climb per hill repeat.

16
00:01:20.944 --> 00:01:26.978
Check rerun: the quality alert is gone. Push to the Garmin calendar, without duplicates.

17
00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:30.472
Then it reads the calendar back to verify.

18
00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:34.830
A computed, tested second opinion. Not a model's hunch.

19
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.806
To go further: the “Guardrails” page of the documentation.
